    <string>Exact Final Cut Pro 12.3 static inspection. The stock pre-injection executable SHA-256 is patcher provenance because the copied host receives one reviewed load command and a new signature. The runtime independently requires the exact copied bundle path, receipt-compatible bundle identifier, unchanged MAS receipt path and SHA-256, version, build, active-slice UUID, and nested ProOnboardingFlowModelOne framework path, SHA-256, active-slice UUID, Objective-C type, and original setter IMP before forwarding that setter with one main-queue asynchronous nil-metadata provider. The only additional replacement is the CCFirstLaunchHelper instance method at arm64 offset 0x924e8 and x86_64 offset 0xc74c0; static inspection pins its PEAppController send at arm64 0x3b648 and x86_64 0x4f1ad, the independent continuation, and the completion-only listener routes at arm64 0x3c32c and x86_64 0x503c8. Its replacement returns without accessing the completion block. The reviewed nested-block encoding is v24@0:8@?&lt;v@?@&quot;NSError&quot;&gt;16. On this supported Objective-C runtime, method_getNumberOfArguments parses that extended encoding as twelve rather than the receiver, selector, and block slots, so the Cloud guard omits an argument-count condition while retaining exact full-encoding, void-return, copied-image, UUID, and architecture-specific original-IMP checks. Schema 10 additionally admits one launcher-flagged disposable-library bootstrap only after NSApplicationDidFinishLaunchingNotification. It pins FFLibraryDocument initWithURL:createDefaultEvent:error: to the exact Flexo image, SHA-256, slice UUID, ABI, and arm64/x86_64 offsets; requires the one canonical absent target, no symlink path components, zero active libraries before creation, public NSDocument registration/presentation, exactly one postcreate active library, and canonical path/device/inode/persistent UID provenance. It never overwrites, removes, retries, opens another library path, imports media, or creates a project fixture.</string>
